        <mxCell id="c65" value="Risks" style="rounded=0;arcSize=6;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F2F3F4;strokeColor=#D5D8DC;strokeWidth=1;fontColor=#2C3E50;fontSize=12;fontStyle=0;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacingLeft=6;spacingRight=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="464" y="344" width="70" height="24" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c66" value="&lt;i&gt;Outlined in teal: the four flows through 2060, the receipts held and the applications to invoices, each about 32 million a year, then the credits on paid invoices and the refunds, tens of thousands. In blue: the closing balance rolled forward and the ledger&#x27;s, a few thousand dollars at most (3,413.46). In coral: the difference, which Excel shows as -0.00 because each cell is a floating-point residue far below a cent; the model answer tests it with ABS(x)&amp;lt;0.005. The opening balance of each year is the closing balance above it (D56 is =C61). Columns B (Source, empty in this block) and F (Total) are hidden, and column A is narrower than the workbook&#x27;s.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontColor=#5D6D7E;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=2;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="374" width="860" height="83" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
